ranch then switches the headline to 'Event log partly chained' but appends its text to that anchored detail. The appended text says an edit among the unchained lines is not detected. The banner therefore claims the anchored part is protected and that edits there go unseen. That happens even though the anchor's prefix digest does cover the lines it spans. The test covers this case with the 'short' anchor and checks only the headline and the 'is not detected' phrase.","fix_commit":"3dc53573ffde8e356721386dc750d210fa35525a","id":"F002","line":257,"path":"agentic_preflight/report/audit.py","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"fixed","suggestion":"When the partly-chained warning applies, build its detail from the plain intact banner (_CHAIN_BANNERS['intact']) rather than the anchored one. Or state that only the first N anchored lines are covered.","title":"A short anchor gives a banner that says two opposite things","unit":"U0035"}],"fingerprint":{"base_tree_sha":"cf2ba231293d1b49072e0b30d6650374379b9508","config_sha256":"25363ddc7d586ecf84e8f7f7fa372aa5c9e7aa56e8216e0ac04452b84d670e9c","configuration_supported":true,"diff_sha256":"588bfcf35b96bb04df667937e49f20c78b807b34302e87699560186766c3064c","excluded_files":[],"executor":"command","grounding_sha256":"9ae53b1c3350bc76b072fcf0a6491fd9d23786cd7f32559bc6ece7e12cdf8174","head_tree_sha":"951f8d0d0f7b6384ff2a63523d94a32ef344489b","intent_sha256":"4d985d45ad905eba2deff55b1b82b3d5d797468dc7e93f526179c8d17226ec8d","version":2},"finished_at":"2026-11-19T23:11:16Z","head_sha":"3dc53573ffde8e356721386dc750d210fa35525a","result":{"command":"env AP_REVIEWER_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5 AP_REVIEWER_EFFORT=low uv run python -B docs/examples/reviewers/claude_review.py","coverage":{"cited_units":[],"clean_units":["U0001","U0002","U0003","U0004","U0005","U0006","U0007","U0008","U0009","U0010","U0011","U0012","U0013","U0014","U0015","U0016","U0017","U0018","U0019","U0020","U0021","U0022","U0023","U0024","U0025","U0